<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  rev_ethnicgroup - equality-monitoring column (raw export col 150, "Ethnic group").

  CLASSIFICATION. Ethnicity IS UK GDPR Article 9 special-category data (racial or ethnic
  origin). This column is Tier 4 (Art. 9) per the architecture doc's data-classification
  table, the same tier as the condition narrative and "other condition" columns - not Tier 3
  like rev_gender, which is ordinary personal data.

  WHY THIS WAS NOT BUILT AT SCHEMA-INTAKE, AND WHY IT IS NOW. The WordPress form asks the
  question (confirmed real: docs/Import/Application Data Export(Sheet1).csv column 150,
  right beside Gender at 149), but the intake flow deliberately declined to persist the
  answer pending SDD OQ-027 ("Is ethnic group actually captured? ... if it is not collected,
  the Art. 9 surface narrows" - owner Emily/DPO, gate: before DPIA sign-off). That question
  is resolved by this change: the reviewer directed this column be built, on
  rev_applicant, secured like (in fact more tightly than) rev_gender. The DPIA sign-off
  OQ-027 names is a separate, still-outstanding paperwork step for Emily/DPO to formally
  record - this schema change does not substitute for it.

  HISTORICAL DATA DOES NOT BACKFILL. Applications submitted before this column existed were
  never asked to persist ethnicity, so any round predating this change will show no data
  here regardless of what the form asked at the time.

  OPTION LIST — ground-truthed, not guessed. These six categories and their exact wording
  are read directly off Round 3 Stats.pptx's own "Ethnic Group" chart (chart3.xml), whose
  six percentages sum to exactly 1.0 - the complete, exhaustive set actually used for that
  round's applicants, not an assumed subset. They match the UK's standard high-level (ONS)
  ethnic-group categories plus the equality-monitoring "Prefer not to say" option this
  project already treats as non-optional for rev_gender.

  "Prefer not to say" is a real option, not an absence, for the same reason rev_gender's is:
  an equality-monitoring question that cannot be declined is not a lawful one.
-->
<optionset Name="rev_ethnicgroup" localizedName="Ethnic Group">
  <OptionSetType>picklist</OptionSetType>
  <IsGlobal>1</IsGlobal>
  <IntroducedVersion>1.0.0.0</IntroducedVersion>
  <IsCustomizable>1</IsCustomizable>
  <options>
    <option value="1">
      <labels>
        <label description="White" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <option value="2">
      <labels>
        <label description="Asian or Asian British" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <option value="3">
      <labels>
        <label description="Black, African, Caribbean or Black British" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <option value="4">
      <labels>
        <label description="Mixed or Multiple ethnic groups" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <option value="5">
      <labels>
        <label description="Other ethnic group" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <option value="6">
      <labels>
        <label description="Prefer not to say" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
  </options>
  <Descriptions>
    <Description description="The applicant's ethnic group, collected for equality monitoring and funder reporting only. UK GDPR Article 9 special-category data - never used in scoring or eligibility. Option 6 'Prefer not to say' must always be offered. Building this column resolves SDD OQ-027; formal DPIA sign-off is a separate step for Emily/DPO." languagecode="1033" />
  </Descriptions>
  <displaynames>
    <displayname description="Ethnic Group" languagecode="1033" />
  </displaynames>
</optionset>
